# Intent: the unit gets itself out of a freeze, can never reboot-loop, and a slow I2C part no longer aborts the boot (rebuild of the old 085 self-restart guard and the crash-fix line of 074 on the current base; owner approval 2026-11-13 and docs/design/feature-gap-2026-11-16.md Train 1 item 4). (1) The host's "reboot" system command used to run through Schedule() on the main loop, so a stuck main loop could never run it: it now runs off the receiving task, through the guard, after 300 ms so the log line and the host's ack leave first. (2) The application main loop ticks a counter every second; the motion sensor task (the one task that never waits on the main loop) asks for a restart after 30 s without a tick, once per freeze, never before the first tick (so setup mode and the boot are not counted). (3) THE GUARD (main/hal/maipai_heal.cc): every self-chosen restart goes through maipai_heal_restart, at most 3 an hour counted in flash (heal_n the count, heal_s the window clock in the unit's running seconds, since no clock survives a restart); the fourth is refused, logged and reported as a "heal" event (action=refused) and as heal_hold=1 in the "boot" event until the hour ends. The restart runs on its own task with an internal 4 KB stack: a flash write from a task whose stack is in PSRAM (the motion and head touch tasks) aborts the unit, which is the crash line of 074. Panics, wireless updates and the owner's Reset are not counted and never held back. (4) I2cDevice::ReadReg retried: it used to abort on any failed read (ESP_ERROR_CHECK, esp_err_t 0x108 once in five boots on the faces flash, docs/design/faces-gate-2026-11-16.md); it now tries three times, resetting the bus between tries, then logs and returns 0. Not taken from 074: the 3600 s idle-shutdown default and boot-into-agent default (product values; boot already starts the agent in this base) and the keep_awake tool (already present). The 8 s stall record of 069 is dropped (diagnostic only).
# Placement: unit (a basic the robot must do alone; it runs with the host off)
# Upstream: m5stack/StackChan firmware/main/hal/hal_imu.cpp and xiaozhi-esp32/main/application.cc and main/boards/common/i2c_device.cc (MIT); main/hal/maipai_heal.cc and maipai_heal.h are new (the CMake glob picks them up)
# Check after a flash: the host's reboot request logs "HealGuard restarting (host): self-restart 1 of 3 this hour" and the next boot event carries heal_why=host heal_n=1; the fourth request inside an hour logs "restart refused" and a heal event with action=refused, and the boot event says heal_hold=1; a main loop held for 30 s logs "main loop stalled for 30 s" and restarts; the reset line "I2C register read ... failed (try 1 of 3)" appears instead of an abort if a part is slow to answer.
